---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import { RATES_SNAPSHOT } from '../../lib/site';
import { defaultParams, wishesForConfidence, worstCaseWishes } from '../../lib/pity';

const charFresh = defaultParams('character');
const charGuar = { ...charFresh, state: 'guaranteed' as const };
const weaponFresh = defaultParams('weapon');
const weaponFp = { ...weaponFresh, fatePoints: 1 as const };

const scenarios = [
  { label: 'Featured character - fresh 50/50', params: charFresh },
  { label: 'Featured character - guaranteed active', params: charGuar },
  { label: 'Selected weapon - Epitomized Path, 0 fate points', params: weaponFresh },
  { label: 'Selected weapon - 1 fate point', params: weaponFp },
];

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Article',
    headline: 'How Many Wishes for a Guaranteed Character in Genshin Impact?',
    description:
      'The full wish-budget ladder: 180 for a guaranteed character from a fresh 50/50, 160 for a selected weapon, plus 50/90/99% confidence budgets and constellation math.',
    datePublished: '2026-10-11',
    author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'PityHub' },
    publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'PityHub' },
    mainEntityOfPage: 'https://pitycalc.top/guides/how-many-wishes-guaranteed/',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How Many Wishes for a Guaranteed Character in Genshin? (180 · 155 · 80)"
  description={`The Genshin wish-budget ladder: 180 wishes guarantees a character from a fresh 50/50, 160 guarantees your weapon, ~155 gives 90% confidence. Full tables for constellations and refinements. Snapshot ${RATES_SNAPSHOT}.`}
  path="/guides/how-many-wishes-guaranteed/"
  ogType="article"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <div class="container">
    <Breadcrumbs crumbs={[{ href: '/guides/', label: 'Guides' }, { label: 'Wishes for a Guarantee' }]} />
    <article class="prose">
      <span class="overline">Guide</span>
      <h1>How many wishes for a guaranteed 5★?</h1>
      <p>
        “Guaranteed” in Genshin means the mathematical worst case - the budget after which the
        system <i>must</i> hand you the character or weapon you chose. It's the right number for
        zero-risk planning and the wrong number for realistic expectation, because soft pity
        usually delivers far sooner. Here's the whole ladder.
      </p>

      <h2><Icon name="star4" size={19} /> The headline numbers</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><b>180 wishes</b> (28,800 primogems) - hard guarantee of the featured character from a fresh 50/50.</li>
        <li><b>90 wishes</b> - hard guarantee if your next 5★ is already guaranteed (you lost a 50/50).</li>
        <li><b>160 wishes</b> - hard guarantee of your selected weapon with Epitomized Path (1 fate point, v5.0+).</li>
        <li><b>~155 wishes</b> - 90% confidence for the featured character from a fresh 50/50.</li>
        <li><b>~80 wishes</b> - the 50/50 point: a coin-flip at the character.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2><Icon name="table" size={19} /> Every level, computed exactly</h2>
      <p>
        Computed at build time with our engine (pity 0, Radiance on, Epitomized Path on):
      </p>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table class="table">
          <thead><tr><th>Scenario</th><th>50% chance</th><th>90% chance</th><th>99% chance</th><th>Guarantee</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {scenarios.map((s) => (
              <tr>
                <td>{s.label}</td>
                <td class="num-cell">{wishesForConfidence(s.params, 0.5)}</td>
                <td class="num-cell"><b>{wishesForConfidence(s.params, 0.9)}</b></td>
                <td class="num-cell">{wishesForConfidence(s.params, 0.99)}</td>
                <td class="num-cell">{worstCaseWishes(s.params)}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2><Icon name="layers" size={19} /> Constellations and refinements stack the ladder</h2>
      <p>
        Each copy repeats the same ladder. Worst-case budget for a target number of copies
        (starting fresh, guarantees included):
      </p>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table class="table">
          <thead><tr><th>Goal</th><th>Worst-case wishes</th><th>Primogems</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>C0 - first copy of the character</td><td class="num-cell">180</td><td class="num-cell">28,800</td></tr>
            <tr><td>C1 - two copies</td><td class="num-cell">360</td><td class="num-cell">57,600</td></tr>
            <tr><td>C2 - three copies</td><td class="num-cell">540</td><td class="num-cell">86,400</td></tr>
            <tr><td>C6 - seven copies</td><td class="num-cell">1,260</td><td class="num-cell">201,600</td></tr>
            <tr><td>R1 - first copy of the weapon</td><td class="num-cell">160</td><td class="num-cell">25,600</td></tr>
            <tr><td>R5 - five copies of the weapon</td><td class="num-cell">800</td><td class="num-cell">128,000</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="note-src">
        Capturing Radiance (v5.0+) nudges the <i>expected</i> cost down slightly (a ~55% featured
        rate instead of 50%) but never changes the worst case.
      </p>

      <h2><Icon name="scale" size={19} /> Which number should you save for?</h2>
      <p>
        Save to your risk tolerance. The 90% budget ({wishesForConfidence(charFresh, 0.9)} for a
        fresh character) is the community sweet spot: you fail only one plan in ten, and you bank
        the leftover ~25 wishes toward the next target. Full-guarantee savers sleep perfectly but
        hold wishes idle for extra patches - with soft pity, unspent wishes are unearned 5★s.
        Run your own numbers on the <a href="/wishes-needed/">wishes-needed calculator</a>, then
        turn the result into a saving timeline with the
        <a href="/savings-planner/">savings planner</a>.
      </p>

      <p class="note-src">
        All figures from our documented model - see the <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a>.
        Snapshot {RATES_SNAPSHOT}.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
